      "body": "Summary:\n\nThe single-host RL launcher used to assign physical GPUs starting at zero to every spawned role, even when the controller was launched with CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=4,5,6,7. The bootstrap environment for the trainer and generators replaced that parent setting with 0,1 and 2,3. On a shared devgpu this could place a run on GPUs already in use, making startup appear stuck.\n\nRead the controller-visible GPU list before spawning actors and pass it to PerHostProvisioner. Allocate successive slices of that list to the trainer and generators, preserving the specified order. When CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES is absent, retain the previous allocation starting at GPU 0. Reject empty, duplicate, or insufficient device lists before spawning any process. Explicit multi-host mesh allocation retains its existing behavior.\n\nDocument the single-host launch pattern and cover default selection, nonzero/reordered devices, extra visible GPUs, malformed lists, and multi-host behavior with CPU tests.\n\nTest Plan:\n- pytest -q tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_shutdown.py (25 passed)\n- flake8 torchtitan/rl/actors/monarch/provisioning.py tests/rl/unit_tests/cpu/test_shutdown.py\n- git diff --check HEAD\n- Four-GPU toy dense job (from the repository root):\n\n    CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=4,5,6,7 \\\n    VLLM_ALLREDUCE_USE_SYMM_MEM=0 \\\n    VLLM_ALLREDUCE_USE_FLASHINFER=0 \\\n    PYTHONPATH=\"$PWD:${PYTHONPATH:-}\" \\\n    python -m torchtitan.rl.train \\\n      --module torchtitan_recipes.rl.alphabet_sort \\\n      --config rl_grpo_qwen3_0_6b_flex \\\n      --output-dir outputs/rl/alphabet_sort_0_6b_flex_nccl",
